public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) {
        return false;
    }
    while (n > 1) {
        if (n % 3!= 0) {
            return false;
        }
        n = n / 3;
    }
    return true;
}
```
This function uses a simple while loop to check if the input number n is a power of three. It first checks if n is less than or equal to zero, and returns false if it is. Then, it repeatedly divides n by three until n is equal to 1, and checks if the remainder of each division is equal to 0. If any of the remainders are not equal to 0, then n is not a power of three, so the function returns false. Otherwise, it returns true as n must be a power of three. This solution runs in O(log₃n) time, which is more efficient than a brute force solution that would take O(n) time.instructor

